From e4bb76e7f3a566ccf0ad36480382faa3339fb321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:10:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] inert: the global inert attribute

React modal libraries put inert on everything outside the open modal and
expect the browser to make it unreachable. HTMLElement.inert now reflects
the attribute, and Element::is_inert() counts an inert flat tree ancestor
as well as modal dialog blocking, with the blocking modal dialog escaping
the inertness of its ancestors as the spec requires. That keeps inert
content out of focus (focusable areas, sequential navigation and the
focus fixup rule all go through is_inert()).

Hit testing skips inert nodes through a user agent pointer-events rule,
so a click on an inert overlay reaches what is beneath it, as in Chrome.
The accessibility tree leaves out inert subtrees and, while a modal
dialog is open, everything but the dialog and the ancestors that hold
it. Layout learns the blocking dialog from the document's top layer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
